[h1]Trash Manager Revamped[/h1]
[i]The definitive inventory management solution for Avorion — overhauled, actively maintained, and expanded by Stormbox.[/i]

Tired of manually sorting through hundreds of turrets and systems after every combat run? [b]Trash Manager Revamped[/b] lets you bulk-mark low-value items for trash using precise material, rarity, tech, and type filters — then sell everything through the game's normal merchant trash flow in one click.

[b]Items are never instantly deleted.[/b] They are flagged safely for reversible selling later. You are always in full control.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]✨ Features[/h2]

[h3]🎯 Precision Bulk Marking[/h3]
Configure exactly what gets marked using independent, stackable filters:
[list]
[*][b]System Rarity[/b] — Mark system upgrades at or below any selected rarity tier. Set to [i]None[/i] to skip systems entirely.
[*][b]Turret Rarity Per Material[/b] — Each material (Iron → Avorion) has its own enable checkbox and rarity dropdown. Thresholds apply equally to turrets and turret blueprints of the same material.
[*][b]Tech Level Range (Optional)[/b] — Narrow the sweep to a Min/Max tech level (1–52). Works with vanilla and modded tech ranges. Turrets and blueprints use [code]averageTech[/code]; systems skip this filter automatically.
[*][b]Item Type Toggles[/b] — Three independent checkboxes let you enable or disable [b]Turrets[/b], [b]Systems[/b], and [b]Templates[/b] (blueprints) as categories. Uncheck any to skip it entirely during all operations.
[/list]

[h3]🗂️ Turret Blueprint (Template) Support[/h3]
Turret blueprints stored in inventory are treated as a fully supported first-class item category. They respect the same per-material rarity thresholds as normal turrets and are reported separately in all Preview and Mark feedback.

[h3]🔍 Safe Preview Mode[/h3]
Before committing anything, hit [b]Preview[/b] for a complete dry-run. It reports exactly how many [b]Turrets[/b], [b]Systems[/b], and [b]Templates[/b] would be marked under the current filter — with a per-category breakdown — without touching your inventory.

[h3]↩️ Surgical Undo — Unmark Filter[/h3]
Made a marking mistake? The new [b]Unmark Filter[/b] button reverses only the items that match your [i]current[/i] active filter. Everything else stays in the trash bin untouched. [b]Unmark All[/b] is still available for a full unconditional rollback.

[h3]🏦 Consolidate Inventory to Vault[/h3]
One button instantly transfers all unequipped, non-favorite turrets, blueprints, and system upgrades from your [b]private inventory[/b] directly into the [b]Alliance Vault[/b]. Favorites are always skipped. If the vault is completely full, excess items are dropped safely near your ship in space rather than lost.

[h3]💾 Persistent Filter Presets — 3 Slots[/h3]
Save your entire filter configuration to one of [b]3 named preset slots[/b] per character. Each slot captures item type toggles, all rarity thresholds, alliance mode, and tech level bounds. Presets are stored server-side and survive session restarts, ship changes, and server logins.

[h3]📊 Live Inventory Stats Bar[/h3]
A real-time bar at the top of the window always shows [b]total items | trashed | favorites[/b] for the active inventory. Automatically refreshed after every Mark, Unmark, Preview, and Consolidate operation.

[h3]🤝 Private & Alliance Inventory[/h3]
All marking, unmarking, and preview operations fully support both private and alliance inventories. A single checkbox in the UI switches the active scope. Clear chat messages are shown when alliance access is unavailable.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]🛡️ Safety[/h2]

The mod [b]never[/b] marks: items in your [b]favorites[/b], already-trashed items, items that fail rarity/material/tech/type filter checks, or vanilla resource items. Accidental cleanup is, by design, nearly impossible.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

Not compatible with any other Trash Manager versions — including the original and rifted versions.
[b]Cosmic Overhaul[/b] — Already built in. Do not install separately alongside Cosmic Overhaul.

